/**
 * Two independent time axes on a business fact — the mixin behind §5.2.
 *
 * A launch control tower is asked two different questions about the past and they
 * have different answers:
 *
 * <ul>
 *   <li><b>Valid time</b> — "what was the Puurs FP release date *for the month of
 *       March*?" This is when the fact was true in the world, carried by
 *       {@link Bitemporal#validFrom} / {@link Bitemporal#validTo}.</li>
 *   <li><b>Transaction time</b> — "when did *we first know* Puurs would slip?"
 *       This is when the system learned the fact, carried by
 *       {@link Bitemporal#recordedAt} / {@link Bitemporal#supersededAt}.</li>
 * </ul>
 *
 * Both are required by R-TR-04, and R-TR-05 turns them into two UI capabilities:
 * replaying the whole portfolio as it stood on a date (valid time), and dating the
 * moment a slip became known (transaction time). A single `lastModified` column
 * cannot answer either question, which is why this mixin exists.
 *
 * <h3>How rows retire</h3>
 * The *current* version of a fact has a null {@link Bitemporal#supersededAt}: it is
 * what the system believes today. Superseding never edits history — it stamps the
 * outgoing row's `supersededAt` and appends a new row. A point-in-time query is
 * therefore "the row whose valid window contains the business date and whose
 * `recordedAt` ≤ the as-of instant and whose `supersededAt` is null or later than
 * it", which is exactly what {@link TemporalQueryService#asOf} implements.
 *
 * Mixed into {@link EntityVersion}, which stores the retired snapshots, and into
 * the governed business entities whose history the demo replays.
 */
type Bitemporal {
  /** UTC instant from which this fact is true in the world. */
  validFrom: datetime

  /**
   * UTC instant at which this fact stops being true in the world. Null means "still
   * true" — an open-ended valid window.
   */
  validTo: datetime

  /** UTC instant the system recorded this fact. Never back-dated; this is the audit-honest one. */
  recordedAt: datetime

  /**
   * UTC instant a later revision replaced this fact. Null marks the row the system
   * currently believes. Set — never cleared — when a new version is appended.
   */
  supersededAt: datetime
}
